    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Swimming-Assistant-Head-Coach_R4129": {
      "title": "Swimming Assistant Head Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. We are seeking an assistant head coach for Marymount University Swimming Team! Job Description: Assistant Head Coach, Swimming Supervisor:  Head Coach, Swimming Location:  Marymount University, Arlington, VA Classification:  Full-time, Exempt Division:  NCAA Division III / Atlantic East Conference Position Overview: As the  Assistant Head Coach for Swimming , you will play a leadership role in advancing the goals of the program by supporting the Head Coach in all areas, including coaching, recruiting, student-athlete development, and administrative management. You are expected to embody Marymount University’s mission and the values of Division III athletics—academic excellence, integrity, leadership, and community engagement. Primary Responsibilities: Coaching & Player Development Collaborate with the Head Coach on the planning and execution of practices, training sessions, and meet strategies. Deliver technical, tactical, and physical training to student-athletes. Provide in-meet coaching support. Recruiting Identify and evaluate prospective student-athletes who meet academic and athletic standards at Marymount. Maintain consistent communication with recruits, families, and club/high school coaches. Plan and conduct campus visits, tours, and recruiting events. Track recruiting activities and manage profiles using platforms such as Front Rush. Student-Athlete Support Foster a positive team culture focused on mutual respect, personal accountability, and inclusive excellence. Provide mentorship and support to student-athletes, emphasizing academic achievement and character development. Assist with monitoring academic progress and collaborate with academic support staff as needed. Encourage student involvement in leadership programs, campus events, and community service. Program Administration Assist with the day-to-day operations of the program: Travel planning and logistics Equipment inventory and uniform management Ensure full compliance with  NCAA, Atlantic East Conference , and  Marymount University  rules and policies. OTHER DUTIES AND ASSIGNMENTS Support departmental events, fundraising initiatives, alumni engagement, and social media efforts. Performs other duties as assigned. Key Expectations: Uphold Marymount University’s mission, including its Catholic identity, commitment to liberal arts education, and dedication to developing ethical leaders. Always maintain professionalism and confidentiality. Represent the university with integrity in all public-facing activities, including recruiting and competition. Communicate effectively with athletic department staff, faculty, student-athletes, and external stakeholders. Work flexible hours, including evenings, weekends, and travel during the competitive season and recruitment periods. Qualifications: Required: Bachelor’s degree 3+ years of coaching experience at the collegiate or elite club level Understanding of NCAA Division III rules and philosophy Valid driver’s license and ability to travel with the team Preferred: Master’s degree Experience with NCAA Division III recruiting and compliance systems Familiarity with Front Rush, Hudl, and Google Workspace CPR/First Aid certification JOB REQUIREMENTS Education                                            Bachelor’s degree. Experience                                         At least 3 years of coaching experience, ideally intercollegiate coaching experience. Collegiate competition experience desired. Thorough knowledge of NCAA regulations and guidelines governing the recruitment and retention of student athletes. Licenses or Certifications             CPR, First Aid and AED certification. Financial Responsibility                Processes or records financial transactions within established guidelines and safeguards. Reviews and/or approves financial transactions for the men’s & women’s swim program. Submit purchase requests and budgetary questions to the business manager to help in the decision process to live within a set budget for the program. Supervision                                        Training/coaching other employees. Scheduling and providing daily work direction to the assistant coaching staff members. Special Knowledge                         Basic computer skills, including ability to utilize Microsoft applications and recruiting/compliance software (Front rush). Special Working Conditions Ability to lift up 50 pounds.  May be required to work when the university is closed.  Ability to work nights, weekends, and some holidays Please note that this role is based in Arlington, VA. Position will be open until filled. Compensation/Total Rewards The salary for this position is $26,500. It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework, ensuring your skills and experience are recognized and rewarded. But your total compensation goes well beyond your salary. As a valued member of our team, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. This includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; FSA or HSA; employee assistance program; life insurance; short- and long-term disability; contributions to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan; financial planning; identity theft protection; pet insurance; credit union and more. Interested in continuing your education? Our tuition remission program supports your professional growth and lifelong learning, and is also open to covered dependents.  On top of that, our generous paid time off plan gives you the flexibility to recharge and maintain balance in your personal and professional life.   Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Housekeeping-and-Events-Setup_R4156": {
      "title": "Housekeeping and Events Setup",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence.       JOB SUMMARY The Facilities Management Department is looking for a Housekeeping and Events Setup Worker for Custodial Services. Entry-level position includes facilities cleaning and events setup duties. Pick-up trash including weekends. Setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for events. Perform other duties as required. Work ethic will include excellent cleaning skills, quality controls, and teamwork. The successful candidate will possess a passion for their work and believe in the mission of Marymount University.  Direct Supervisor Custodial Supervisor Status: Full-time (Hourly) Division  Main Campus Facilities Management Department Target Weekly Hours 40   Location:      Main Campus Benefits Eligibility Yes MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Cleaning of facilities and trash removal. Setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for events. Communicates with University management, customers, and staff to ensure needs are met and cleaning standards are achieved. Performs cleaning service requests and event setup requirements. Uses the required supplies and equipment made available to staff to meet quality cleaning standards. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Communicates effectively and respectfully with staff, customers, and the University community. Works under the direct supervision of the Custodial Supervisor. Physical condition adequate to perform job functions. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. on a regular basis. Non-shift hours, weekend, and holiday work may be required. Driving of University vehicle may be required. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma preferred. Minimum of 2 years of related work experience or equivalent combination of education and work experience preferred. Possession of or ability to obtain a valid Driver’s License upon employment preferred. Good driving record. Successful completion of background check upon employment. Preferred Qualifications Industry certification Janitor University Certification Experience in using commercial cleaning equipment  The hourly rate for the position is $16.00.   It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework, ensuring your skills and experience are recognized and rewarded. But your total compensation goes well beyond your salary. As a valued member of our team, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. This includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; FSA or HSA; employee assistance program; life insurance; short- and long-term disability; contributions to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan ; financial planning; identity theft protection; pet insurance ; credit union and more. Interested in continuing your education? Our tuition remission program supports your professional growth and lifelong learning , and is also open to covered dependent s.   On top of that, our generous paid time off plan gives you the flexibility to recharge and maintain balance in your personal and professional life.          Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Temporary-Part-Time-Campus-Safety-Officer-II_R3818": {
      "title": "Temporary Part Time Campus Safety Officer II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. We are seeking a Temporary Part Time Campus Safety Officer II who will be expected to provide for the safety of students, faculty, staff; and to protect/secure University grounds, buildings, and parking facilities against theft, illegal entry, and damage. Demonstrate quick and decisive responses to incidents. Assist training other Campus Safety Officers. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES ● Serves as a deterrent to a criminal event and conduct as a protector of the campus community. ● Enforces all University rules, regulations and policies as well as assisting with assisting with similar actions regarding local, state and federal laws. ● Maintains high visibility and patrols buildings, grounds and parking facilities to secure and protect University property. ● Responds to any emergency and assists all responding emergency services personnel during their respective responses; responds to all other incidents, complaints, alarms, fires, vehicle crashes, disturbances, assaults, robberies as well as any other requests for service on the relevant campuses. ● Files reports for all crimes, rules and policy violations, damage to property, suspicious activity, miscellaneous problems, or any other unusual incident or occurrence. ● Monitors and assists with traffic and parking rules and regulations violations; which may include the movement of vehicles within restricted area(s); may direct traffic as required. ● Maintain communications contact between officers, supervisors and communications base while on duty via two-way radio, cellular telephone or other as approved and may be necessary. ● Locks and unlocks all facilities and activates or deactivates alarms as scheduled and/or instructed. OTHER DUTIES AND ASSIGNMENTS ● Reviews all reports, emails, messages, notices and directives from all previous shifts; receives briefing from shift supervisor; reviews current campus calendar and activities, and all other pertinent documents and information at the beginning of each shift. ● Conduct field investigations, follow-up investigations, interviews as directed/required and complete detailed reports which reflect the results of those actions that would be capable of fully informing relevant other campus departments/personnel of information which may be utilized for the betterment and service of the campus community. ● Is fully knowledgeable of all campus buildings, departments, functions, and grounds. ● Maintains a proper personal appearance at all times when on duty. Standards include neatly trimmed hair and facial hair and proper hygiene. ● Maintains all quality and professional standards within the Campus Safety department. Reports any standards not being met. ● Fill on a as needed basis, on various shifts and/or in four hour (minimum) blocks of time, scheduling vacancies of all types, as well as scheduling needs that may develop as a result of special events and other situations that may require additional personnel. ● Performs other duties as may be assigned. JOB REQUIREMENTS Education High School graduate or GED required, Associate’s degree or Bachelor's degree preferred. Experience 2+ years of experience working in law enforcement, security department or equivalent. Higher education experience preferred Driving Requirements Must have a valid driver’s license and a clean Motor Vehicle Record (MVR). A good driving record, as reported by the Department of Transportation, is essential. Must hold, or be able to obtain, all applicable licenses required by governing authorities to operate a commercial vehicle. Adheres to local and state laws, as well as brand and owner guidelines for driver certification and safe transport of guests. No texting or use of cell phones while the vehicle is in motion. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities ● Strong interpersonal skills, including written and oral communication skills ● Comfort dealing with ambiguity and the ability to work independently ● Ability to make critical safety decisions independently when no supervisor is available ● Familiarity with preventive patrols, investigations, report writing, and community-oriented problem-solving interactions. ● Demonstrated an ability to calm situations. ● Demonstrated appropriate reactions to nuanced and/or escalating situations. ● Demonstrated quick and decisive responses to incidents. ● Demonstrated timely use of the department’s procedures and processes. Licenses or Certifications Campus Safety Officer Certification or ability to obtain certification within 6 months from Virginia Department of Criminal Justices Service (DCJS), Basic First Aid and CPR preferred. Financial Responsibility No. Supervision No. Special Knowledge Is fully knowledgeable and capable of all laws as they pertain to Campus Safety, such as the Clery Act, Title IX, and FERPA SPECIAL WORKING CONDITIONS ● Ability to stand or walk (for up to an entire shift) on various surfaces (tile, concrete, etc.) ● Ability to climb stairs, ramps or ladders ● Ability to bend or twist waist, knees and neck to perform various duties ● Ability to lift and carry up to 40 pounds ● Ability to run as needed ● Be able to work outdoors in inclement weather for extended periods of time Please note that this role is in person based in Arlington, VA. Position will be open until filled. Compensation/Total Rewards The hourly rate for this position is $21.77. It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework. Part-time employees are eligible to contribute the university’s 403(b) retirement plan on their own Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Ballston-Center/Associate-Director-of-Admissions_R4079": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-14\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Marymount University is seeking an Assistant/Associate Director for Graduate Admissions to recruit and enroll incoming graduate students in programs on campus or online as part of the overall admission strategic plan. The  Associate Director will effectively represent the University in the graduate student market collaborating with select graduate program faculty at class visits, fairs, conferences, information sessions, webinars, and off-site outreach efforts. The associate Director manages the direct recruitment and enrollment of candidates for graduate programs. Critical components of this position are proactive outreach to potential students to help grow prospects for  enrollment in assigned programs and providing strong support and direction to prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. The associate director is accountable for the recruitment of multiple programs and collaborates with the graduate enrollment team to ensure that the target enrollments for the assigned programs are achieved.  Directly assists the other associate director for graduate admissions and AVP for graduate enrollment  in managing the recruitment process and the delivery of information sessions, presentations, and customized promotional events on-campus and off-campus across all graduate and doctoral programs.  Counsels prospective applicants regarding admission requirements, academic eligibility, program options, residency requirements, and alternative educational choices, where appropriate. Conducts informational interviews, meetings or programs designed to promote admission or higher education. Reviews and enforces academic program requirements and enrollment restrictions for all University schools and colleges. Conducts information session presentations as well as assists in developing off-campus recruiting strategies for domestic school/college fairs and events.  Represents the graduate enrollment office externally and within the assigned colleges, works closely with graduate program directors, and advisors, to devise new and innovative tactics to generate and convert quality leads into enrolled students.  Ability to travel and work occasional evening and weekend hours. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree required; master's degree preferred. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, enrollment management, or higher education student services. Demonstrated experience managing recruitment initiatives, counseling prospective students, and interpreting enrollment data to inform decision-making. Experience using a student information system and CRM, preferably Slate. Preferred Qualifications Three (3) or more years of experience in graduate admissions or graduate enrollment management. Experience supervising professional staff, student workers, or graduate assistants. Experience collaborating with faculty and academic leadership to support enrollment goals. Experience developing and executing enrollment communication and yield strategies. Experience with application review, holistic admissions practices, and graduate recruitment events Please note that this role is hybrid eligible and based in Arlington, VA. Position will be open until filled. Compensation/Total Rewards The salary for this position is up to $70,000, depending on appointment.  It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework, ensuring your skills and experience are recognized and rewarded. But your total compensation goes well beyond your salary. As a valued member of our team, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. This includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; FSA or HSA; employee assistance program; life insurance; short- and long-term disability; contributions to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan; financial planning; identity theft protection; pet insurance; credit union and more. Interested in continuing your education? Our tuition remission program supports your professional growth and lifelong learning, and is also open to covered dependents.  On top of that, our generous paid time off plan gives you the flexibility to recharge and maintain balance in your personal and professional life.   Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Housekeeping-and-Events-Setup--Part-Time-_R4134": {
      "title": "Housekeeping and Events Setup (Part Time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence.     The Facilities Management Department is looking for a Housekeeping and Events Setup Worker for Custodial Services. Entry-level position includes facilities cleaning and events setup duties. Pick-up trash including weekends. Setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for events. Perform other duties as required. Work ethic will include excellent cleaning skills, quality controls, and teamwork. The successful candidate will possess a passion for their work and believe in the mission of Marymount University.  Direct Supervisor Custodial Supervisor Status: Part Time (Hourly) Division  Facilities Target Weekly Hours 29   Location:      Main Campus MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Cleaning of facilities and trash removal. Setup and breakdown of tables, chairs, and other equipment for events. Communicates with University management, customers, and staff to ensure needs are met and cleaning standards are achieved. Performs cleaning service requests and event setup requirements. Uses the required supplies and equipment made available to staff to meet quality cleaning standards. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Communicates effectively and respectfully with staff, customers, and the University community. Works under the direct supervision of the Custodial Supervisor. Physical condition adequate to perform job functions. Must be able to lift 50 lbs. on a regular basis. Non-shift hours, weekend, and holiday work may be required. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma preferred. Minimum of 2 years of related work experience or equivalent combination of education and work experience preferred. Successful completion of background check upon employment. Preferred Qualifications Industry certification Janitor University Certification Experience in using commercial cleaning equipment  Please note that this role is in person   based in Arlington, VA.   Position will be open until filled.     Compensation/Total Rewards   The hourly rate for this position is $16.00. Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
