    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Vice-President-for-Academic-Affairs---Provost_R3773": {
      "title": "Vice President for Academic Affairs & Provost",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Marymount University Vice President for Academic Affairs & Provost Marymount University stands at a pivotal moment in its 75-year history. Founded in 1950 by the Religious of the Sacred Heart of Mary, Marymount has grown from a small, regional women’s college into a nationally recognized, globally connected Catholic university recognized for its academic excellence, commitment to serving others, and preparing its 4,300 students for success. Located in Arlington, Virginia—just minutes from downtown Washington, D.C.—Marymount was the first Catholic university and the first Hispanic-Serving Institution in the Commonwealth, proudly representing the region's diversity and vibrancy. Today, Marymount is a university on the rise. The institution recently earned dual national distinctions from the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education and the American Council on Education—placing it among just 33 universities nationwide recognized for both research excellence and expanding access and opportunity. Marymount has also been named a Best National University and the top-ranked private institution in Virginia by U.S. News & World Report , and one of Forbes ’ 2026 America’s Top Colleges—a testament to its growing reputation and transformative impact. As the University welcomes its largest and most diverse incoming class in history and launches Momentum: The Campaign for Marymount, a bold $50 million initiative to advance its mission and priorities, the institution is set for an exciting new chapter. With growing research efforts, innovative academic programs, and a track record of social mobility that transforms lives, Marymount offers an environment where purpose and progress intersect. This is a key moment to join a vibrant leadership team guiding a successful institution into its next chapter of growth, innovation, and service. At Marymount, you’ll help shape a university that not only prepares students for success but also inspires them to Learn with Purpose . About the Position The Vice President for Academic Affairs & Provost serves as Marymount’s Chief Academic Officer and a key member of the President’s Cabinet—playing an essential role in shaping the university’s academic vision, fostering a culture of excellence, and advancing its mission to prepare workforce-ready students. Reporting directly to the President, the Provost provides executive leadership and strategic oversight for the university’s academic programs, faculty, and research efforts. The Provost collaborates with deans, faculty, and campus leaders to identify innovative curriculum and market-driven programs that are relevant to our region, promote academic innovation, enhance student success, and elevate Marymount’s national reputation for excellence and accessibility. This senior leader will oversee and support the academic mission of the University, fostering a collegial and innovative community built on trust, shared governance, and a commitment to the mission. Marymount’s academic enterprise includes three colleges and numerous schools and centers: College of Business, Innovation, Leadership & Technology (BILT) – home to the Schools of Business, Design and Art, and Technology and Innovation, as well as the Center for the Innovative Workforce. College of Health and Education – encompassing the Schools of Counseling, Education, Health Sciences, and the Malek School of Nursing Professions, along with the Center for Optimal Aging. College of Sciences and Humanities – including the Schools of Humanities, Science, Mathematics & Engineering, and Social and Behavioral Sciences. In addition, administrative areas within academic affairs include: Library and Learning Services; Academic Finance; Accreditation, Planning and Institutional Effectiveness; Student Health & Wellness; Registrar; Student Success and Support Services. The successful candidate must be tenured and possess the highest caliber of character, integrity, and trustworthiness, combined with vision, initiative, and energy to promote academic excellence and student success. Serving as a strategic advisor to the President and a visible advocate for faculty and academic life, the Provost will help steer Marymount through a period of significant growth—leading with purpose, innovation, and a steadfast dedication to student-centered learning. Key Attractors: Transformational Leadership Opportunity: An influential role to lead, elevate, and shape the academic mission of a top private university in the Washington, D.C., area—an institution with record enrollment, nationwide recognition, and historic momentum. Strategic Influence & Impact: As the chief academic officer, the Provost will play a crucial role in shaping the future of a dynamic, mission-driven university whose faculty, staff, students, and alumni are making a significant impact locally, nationally, and globally. Academic Excellence & Collaboration: Lead a community of committed scholars and educators dedicated to delivering excellent teaching and student success. Foster a collegial environment of shared governance, innovation, and continuous improvement. Empowered Leadership & Faculty Development: Ability to recruit, develop, and support top-tier faculty, as well as to improve academic programs that meet the needs of today’s students and future industries. Marymount’s tradition of excellence is enhanced by its commitment to modern facilities, cutting-edge technology, and support for faculty innovation. Accreditation and Compliance: Oversee the accreditation processes for all our academic programs, ensuring compliance with SACSCOC standards and with specialized accrediting bodies relevant to each discipline. This involves coordinating institutional efforts and aligning program outcomes with accreditation criteria across the board. A Community and a Place to Thrive: Located in Arlington, Virginia—just minutes from downtown D.C.—Marymount offers the ideal blend of professional opportunities and quality of life. The region’s exceptional schools, cultural vitality, and diverse neighborhoods create an outstanding environment for both professional and personal growth. The Provost will join a collaborative leadership team and a warm, inclusive community where ideas are heard; innovation is encouraged, and purpose drives progress. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Commitment to building a strong and innovative learning environment for students that stresses academic quality, student engagement, experiential learning, and global perspectives. Oversee the top accreditations for all academic programs, including SACSCOC. Ability to lead a community with sensitivity through a time of significant growth and change. A nuanced understanding of student retention strategies, student academic support services, and assessment. Exceptional budgetary and financial management skills, and the ability to share financial information clearly and transparently. The ability to set high standards and inspire others is important. Qualifications Required: Tenured with a doctorate (PhD) or terminal degree from an accredited institution. A distinguished record of academic achievement and leadership in higher education, typically at the dean or provost level. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible academic administrative experience; minimum of 5 years of teaching experience; at least 3 years in a Chair or Dean position. Excellent teaching record. Demonstrated success in leading academic innovation, managing complex budgets, and fostering collaborative teams. Commitment to shared governance, faculty development, and student-centered education. Preferred: Understanding of the challenges and opportunities facing higher education. Experience with regional and program-specific accreditation. Familiarity with online and hybrid learning environments and educational technologies. Personal Characteristics Visionary, strategic thinker with strong communication and interpersonal skills. Transparent and collaborative leadership style. Commitment to academic excellence, integrity, and lifelong learning. Ability to build consensus and manage change effectively. Please note that this role is an in-person position based in Arlington, VA. To Apply: Qualified candidates are invited to submit a C.V. and cover letter addressing qualifications related to the aforementioned responsibilities and competencies to : Jenessa Hoffman, President of Recruiting, via email at  jhoffman@esgi-pr.com .  While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been appointed, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by August 31, 2026 to receive optimal consideration. Compensation/Total Rewards The salary range for this position is $265,000 - $285,000, commensurate with experience and discipline. It is also competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework. Salary is only one aspect of an employee’s total compensation. Total rewards include: comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life insurance, supplemental life insurance, short/long term disability, EAP, credit union, a tuition remission program, contribution to the University’s 403B retirement plan, 457 plan, paid time off and more. Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty---Graphic---Media-Design_R4132": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Graphic + Media Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Title                                        Adjunct Faculty Direct Supervisor    GMD Program Manager Status Part-Time, Exempt Division Academic Affairs T arget Weekly Hours     10 Location      Main Campus Benefits Eligibility             No JOB SUMMARY The School of Design + Art in the College of Business, Innovation, Leadership, and Technology (BILT) at Marymount University invites applications from persons qualified to teach undergraduate GMD studio courses. Depending on your expertise and experience, you may teach a course in any area of study offered by the GMD program, including Adobe CC, digital photography, videography, motion graphics, digital publishing or publications, web design, UX/UI, or design communications. Applicants will be expected to follow the syllabus and set curriculum for the course already prepared and delivered through Canvas. Faculty are expected to teach high-quality courses in face-to-face settings. The School of Design + Art within the College of BILT is located at Marymount University’s Main Campus in the city of Arlington, Virginia. Our college is committed to preparing students for the industries in our community from startups to large established companies. Marymount University welcomes and values all members of our community. Guided by the mission of our founders, the Religious of the Sacred Heart of Mary (RSHM), to achieve unity through diversity, Marymount honors our diversity as a source of strength. Our differences inspire intellectual curiosity and collectively allow us to tackle the challenges of the world. We seek to foster an inclusive community in which each person’s race, ethnicity, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, veteran status, age, ability, class, national origin, and immigration status are fully respected and celebrated. According to the vision of the RSHM that “ALL may have life, and have it to the FULL,” we strive to create an atmosphere of mutual respect, cooperation, and civility where all community members are S.A.I.N.T.S—Safe, Accepted, Included, Needed, Treasured, and Seen. Please submit a letter of interest; a current C.V.; and a portfolio of no more than 20 images (10 professional, 10 student work) in PDF format, or a link to a digital portfolio of professional and student work.   Professional Websites are accepted as well. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Teach designated courses, including keeping teaching materials current, interacting with students in discussions and hands-on activities, the continuous grading of assignments, and monitoring student performance through the courses. Maintain appropriate office hours and support students in their educational journey and in their career progression. Work with the GMD Program Manager to identify new subjects in the field and identify yourself or other guest speakers and potential adjuncts to deliver this material.   EDUCATION & EXPERIENCE REQUIREMENTS Masters degree and/or substantial professional experience in the design industry Five years of professional experience in the field is preferred Must be proficient in design software and processes using Adobe CC in a Mac environment. Experience teaching in higher education is preferred   Compensation /Benefits   Adjuncts receive   remuneration   on a semester   basis, pay is   $1,200 /credit hour . They may make their own contribution to a 403b retirement plan.    Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Executive-Director---Center-for-Democracy---Free-Enterprise_R4133": {
      "title": "Executive Director - Center for Democracy & Free Enterprise",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Position Summary Marymount University seeks a founding Executive Director to shape and lead the Center for Democracy and Free Enterprise as a national platform for leadership development, entrepreneurial capacity, and expanded participation in capital and ownership systems. This role is for a builder. The Executive Director will translate the University's vision for the center into an operational, financially sustainable, and nationally recognized model that connects talent with enterprise, capital, and opportunities in institutional leadership. The Executive Director will serve as the chief architect, operator, and external ambassador responsible for strategy, partnerships, fundraising, and execution. About the Center The Center for Democracy and Free Enterprise forms ethical leaders and renews the nation's founding promise that opportunity, enterprise, and self-government belong to all. Grounded in Marymount's Catholic tradition and its commitment to educating the whole person, the Center treats enterprise and economic participation not as ends in themselves but as pathways to opportunity, service, and human flourishing. The Center prepares students to lead with both competence and conscience: to build and steward enterprises, to widen access to capital and ownership and to participate in democracy as responsible citizens. It creates direct pipelines from the classroom to the marketplace, equipping students to launch startups and new ventures that make meaningful contributions to society and open avenues of growth for America. It is private enterprise, innovation, and entrepreneurship that will increasingly shape the country's future. Marymount intends for its graduates to help build it. In doing so, the center advances Marymount's vision of becoming a leading Catholic university recognized for innovation and student success. Key Responsibilities 1. Strategic Leadership & Center Development Design and implement the Center’s multi-year strategy aligned with the University’s mission Build a scalable model integrating leadership development, entrepreneurship, and market access Establish the Center as a national exemplar of applied, nontraditional academic programming Define success metrics tied to leadership outcomes, enterprise creation, and economic participation 2. Program Design & Execution Launch integrated programs focused on: Leadership development Entrepreneurial capability Capital and market fluency Ownership pathways Ensure programming is practical, experience-based, and connected to real economic systems Oversee curriculum partnerships, external engagement, and applied learning experiences 3. Partnerships & Ecosystem Building Build strategic relationships with: Corporations and industry leaders Investment firms and capital networks Entrepreneurs and founders Policy and institutional leaders Create pipelines connecting students to internships, mentorship, funding, and enterprise opportunities 4. Fundraising & Resource Development Lead all fundraising efforts, including: Major gifts and naming opportunities Corporate partnerships Foundation grants Translate the Center’s mission into a compelling investment case for donors Partner with university advancement to secure long-term financial sustainability 5. Institutional Leadership & Visibility Position the Center as a national voice on economic participation and enterprise development Represent the Center in public forums, media, and thought leadership platforms Work closely with university leadership to align the Center with Marymount’s broader strategy ​ 6. Team Building & Operations Recruit and lead a high-performing team Manage budget, operations, and program outcomes Establish efficient processes and strong governance practices Qualifications 10–15+ years of leadership experience in one or more of the following: Entrepreneurship / venture building Finance / investment / capital markets Corporate leadership Public-private partnerships Demonstrated experience building organizations, initiatives, or platforms from concept to scale Proven fundraising and relationship development success Strong understanding of how capital, markets, and institutions function Exceptional communication and external-facing leadership skills Key Success Metrics Funds raised and long-term financial sustainability Number and strength of strategic relationships with corporations, investors, financial institutions, venture capital firms, angel networks, philanthropic funds, community development finance organizations, or corporate investment groups that provides students and entrepreneurs access to funding, investment expertise, and pathways to business formation and growth. Student outcomes (placements, ventures launched, leadership trajectories) National visibility and influence of the Center Scalable program model with replicable impact Reporting Structure Reports to: Provost Works closely with: Advancement, academic leadership, and external advisory board Please note that this role is a hybrid position, with the onsite portion being on the main campus. The position will be open until filled. Compensation The Executive Director’s compensation will include the base salary, performance bonus, and the health insurance, retirement benefits, and tuition remission offered to other employees. The base salary for the position will be $130,000 per year. The size of the performance bonus will be based on the success of the Executive Director’s work, including fundraising, community outreach, strategic partnerships, and overall program performance. As a valued member of our team, you’ll enjoy a comprehensive benefits package designed to support your health, financial security, and work-life balance. This includes medical, dental, and vision coverage;   FSA or HSA; employee assistance program;   life insurance; short- and long-term disability;   contributions to the University’s 403(b) retirement plan ; financial   planning; identity   theft protection; pet insurance ; credit union and more.   Interested in continuing your education? Our tuition remission program supports your professional growth and lifelong learning , and is also open to covered dependent s.     On top of that, our generous paid time off plan gives you the flexibility to recharge and maintain balance in your personal and professional life.    Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
