    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Adjunct-Lab-Instructor_R3754": {
      "title": "Adjunct Lab Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Title                                         Adjunct Lab Instructor Direct Supervisor   Director of Lab and Experiential Learning              Status                                     Non- exempt                             Division                                  Academic Affairs                         Location      Marymount University Main Campus Benefits Eligibility             No JOB SUMMARY Marymount University is seeking dedicated and skilled Nursing Lab and Simulation Instructors to join our team in preparing the next generation of nurses. Lab and simulation faculty play a vital role in shaping the clinical skills, confidence, and professional growth of our students—helping them transition from learners to colleagues in the nursing profession. Under the supervision of the Director of Lab and Experiential Learning, Nursing Lab Instructors: Deliver instruction in nursing clinical skills and provide technical support during simulation. Support lab readiness and smooth operation of skills labs and simulation scenarios. Contribute to student learning through instruction, mentorship, and facilitation of hands-on experiences. Assist with lab operations including maintaining supplies, ensuring equipment functionality, and supporting safe, effective learning environments. This role combines teaching, technical support, and professional collaboration to make a lasting impact on student success and the future of the nursing profession. Physical Requirements: The position requires the ability to lift loads in excess of 50 pounds. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the job. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Set up equipment, supplies and mannequins for clinical skills demonstrations according to established simulation guidelines. Assist Faculty, Simulation Technician, and Lab Director in the preparation, use, monitoring, and maintenance of the nursing labs and simulation manikins. Facilitation of faculty-supervised simulated nursing activities for students. Provides initial or remedial instruction in nursing clinical skills and simulation for students. Provide a safe, secure, and comfortable lab environment for students by keeping lab equipment clean and in good working order. Assist students with supplemental instructional media. OTHER DUTIES AND ASSIGNMENTS Perform administrative tasks under the direction of the Director of Lab and Experiential Learning JOB REQUIREMENTS Education                                      To perform this job successfully, the individual must possess a MSN degree, hold a current Virginia RN license, possess a minimum of one year of experience, and be physically able to perform essential duties. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Experience                                   2-3 years of teaching experience and/or professional experience in nursing; experience in student advising and teaching pre-service nurses in a university setting. Financial Responsibility          None Supervision                                  None SPECIAL WORKING CONDITIONS The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential function: Ability to lift loads in excess of 50 pounds. Compensation /Benefits   The hourly pay rate for this adjunct position is $37.50. Adjunct Instructors may make their own contribution to a 403b retirement plan. Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Athletics-Bus-Driver---Part-Time-1_R3446": {
      "title": "Athletics Bus Driver - Part Time-1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. Marymount University welcomes applications for the position of Athletics Bus Driver. This position will report directly to the Athletics Business Manager. The Bus driver is a part-time hourly position with the responsibilities of transporting our student-athletes, coaches and staff to and from practice and events that occur off campus.  Adherence to institutional, conference, and NCAA Division III policies and procedures is required. Clean Class B CDL License with passenger endorsements is required. The candidate must be familiar with DOT rules and requirements. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES ​ Transportation of students, coaches and staff to practice and competition venues (90%) Ability to work with google documents, check and respond to e-mail and phone calls. Training on google docs will be provided (5%) Must keep written log of activity transportation for all University events (3%) Help with light cleaning and inform supervisor when maintenance is needed (2%) Transport sports teams and students to off-campus events and practices from mid-August thru end of May; hours per week will vary during playing seasons and dependent on driver availability. Must be able to adapt to a flexible schedule; hours and days will vary depending on athletic schedules; nights and weekends are required.  A pool of drivers will create flexibility and drivers will submit their availability for scheduling purposes. Bus: 2022 Eldorado Advantage XL 40 International bus 8 feet wide and 40.5 feet long. Full cab – driver OEM seating. Max 36 passengers with full width back storage area (outside access). GPS unit to determine best route to destination provided on itinerary. JOB REQUIREMENTS Education                                           High School degree or GED Experience             Familiar   with DOT rules   and requirements. Ability to read basic instructions, road signs and maps, and be able to keep a written log of activity. Strong communications skills including the ability to communicate by   telephone/e-mail/text. Strong customer service abilities with emphasis on customer satisfaction Strong organizational & Time management skills Positive attitude with a professional appearance Willingness to learn and be coached as needed Collegiate or scholastic transportation experience preferred. Licenses or   Certifications             Valid Class B CDL with passenger endorsements. Clean driving record Financial   Responsibility                None Supervision                                          None SPECIAL WORKING CONDITIONS Physical Demands:   The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. The bus driver must be able to operate a 36-passenger bus; Must be able to sit for long periods while operating the vehicle; Must be able to negotiate traffic patterns; Must be able to withstand standard traffic and passenger noise Ability to lift more than 50 pound Ability to work nights, weekends, and some holidays Mental Demands Maintain professional attitude and demeanor in difficult situations. Please note that this role is in person based in Arlington, VA. Position will be open until filled. Compensation/Total Rewards The hourly rate for this position is $23.46. It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework. Part-time employees are eligible to contribute the university’s 403(b) retirement plan on their own. Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
    },
    "https://marymount.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Flag-Football-Coach-1_R2784": {
      "title": "Assistant Flag Football Coach-1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt Marymount University, we believe meaningful work happens when talented people come together with shared purpose. We serve not only our students—but one another—creating a culture where teamwork, adaptability, and resilience are part of everyday practice, Located in Arlington, Virginia, just minutes from Washington, D.C., Marymount offers a dynamic and forward-looking environment where innovation is encouraged and flexibility is valued. We understand that higher education is evolving, and we embrace change with creativity, responsiveness, and a solutions-oriented mindset. Our faculty and staff thrive in a community that prioritizes communication, cross-functional collaboration, and service-driven leadership. Whether working directly with students or supporting them behind the scenes, every role contributes to a shared mission: helping students grow, succeed, and lead with purpose and confidence. We are seeking an enthusiastic Assistant Flag Football Coach to assist the Head Coach with recruiting, scouting, and practice planning. MAJOR DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Perform competition day duties as assigned, and monitor equipment inventory and care. Assist with practice and competition day management and activities Assist with organizational planning (travel, community service, study hall, etc.), and support student-athlete development and assist with roster management. Help with the planning and organization of camps and clinics. OTHER DUTIES AND ASSIGNMENTS Know and comply with all Marymount rules and regulations. Must be CPR and First Aid certified. Provide positive leadership for student-athletes. Performs other duties as assigned. JOB REQUIREMENTS Education: Bachelor’s degree, master’s degree preferred. Experience: 1 to 3 years of flag football experience. Licenses or Certifications: CPR and First Aid certified Financial Responsibility: None Supervision: None Special Knowledge: Know and comply with all NCAA rules and regulations, and pass the NCAA Coaches Certification Exam annually. SPECIAL WORKING CONDITIONS Being able to lift up to 50 pounds. Please note that this role is in person based in Arlington, VA. Position will be open until filled. Compensation/Total Rewards This is a stipend-based position: the stipend for this role ranges from $200 to $400, depending on experience and timing within the semester. It is competitive, market-based, and aligned with the University’s financial framework. Part-time employees are eligible to contribute to the university’s 403(b) retirement plan on their own. Qualified candidates are invited to apply via our career portal by submitting a cover letter addressing their qualifications related to the information listed above, along with a resume. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background check and employment verification, and other role related requirements such as motor vehicle and/or drug screening.   Marymount University is an equal opportunity employer. Marymount University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity and expression, marital status, pregnancy, veteran status or any other protected bases under applicable federal and local laws and regulations in any of its programs or its activities, including employment and admission.  The university also expressly prohibits any form of sex discrimination and sexual misconduct including sexual harassment, dating and domestic violence, rape, sexual assault, sexual exploitation and stalking in any of its programs or activities, including employment and admission.  For more information, please visit:  https://marymount.edu/student-life/health-wellness/title-ix-2/ Marymount University is an E-Verify employer. http://marymount.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/04/UTF-8E-Verify_Participation_Poster_Eng_Es-1.pdf"
